<title>CHINA: China tea exports down 2.7 percent in 1996.</title>
<headline>China tea exports down 2.7 percent in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's tea exports fell by 2.7 percent in 1996 to 488,000 tonnes, the China Business Daily said on Thursday quoting an industry report.</p>
<p>Agricultural authorities would relax controls over exports of green tea this year, the report said without elaborating.</p>
<p>Although domestic tea sales rose nine percent to 7.2 billion yuan ($867 million) last year, heavy taxes and poor management had continued to drag down the economic performance of tea enterprises, the report said.</p>
<p>The state purchase price and the domestic market price of tea both rose in 1996, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
